From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 02:55:47 +0200
Subject: media: gc2145: Stop erroring out on read-only control updates

set_fmt() and set_frame_interval() push new values into PIXEL_RATE,
HBLANK and VBLANK with the internal __v4l2_ctrl_s_ctrl() helpers, and
those still call s_ctrl even for read-only controls. There was no case
for any of them, so each update logged "setting unknown control" and
returned -EINVAL. Nothing looked at the return value, but the log
noise was real whenever a format was set while powered.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
@@ -1210,6 +1210,16 @@ static int gc2145_s_ctrl(struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl)
 
 		return gc2145_write(sensor, 0x8d, test2);
 
+	case V4L2_CID_PIXEL_RATE:
+	case V4L2_CID_HBLANK:
+	case V4L2_CID_VBLANK:
+		/*
+		 * Read-only controls that only ever carry values computed
+		 * from the mode. They still reach us through the internal
+		 * s_ctrl helpers used to update them.
+		 */
+		return 0;
+
 #if 0
 	case V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE_METERING:
 		if (val == V4L2_EXPOSURE_METERING_AVERAGE)
